+# Agent Note: Composer official pricing hint
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-08-19-composer-official-pricing-hint.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+The composer needed a small, discoverable reminder about the current DeepSeek peak/off-peak window without changing the existing model and permission controls. Users also needed the current model prices without leaving the composer, while the source page is an external documentation page that is not a reliable browser-side data endpoint.
+
+## Decision
+
+Add a dedicated `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-peak-pricing` plugin package. Its Client half registers the existing `conversation.input.right` slot, so the notice stays between the permission and model controls and remains additive to the core InputBar layout. The notice is centered within the composer card and uses the existing primitives `HoverCard` and design tokens.
+
+The Host half fetches and parses the official DeepSeek pricing page through a same-origin route at `/plugins/deepseek-pricing/data`. The route caches the parsed table for 15 minutes, recalculates the Beijing current period for every response, and returns a visible source link and an error state when the source is unavailable. The Client keeps a shared in-flight request and displays the official table's cache-hit, cache-miss, and output prices for each model version.
+
+The Client resolves the visible notice from the current Beijing period and checks it every 30 seconds, so the anchor changes to `现在是梁文峰时间` on weekdays during 09:00–12:00 or 14:00–18:00, and to `现在是梁文谷时间` during all other periods. The parser treats idle pricing as an invariant: every idle value must equal half of its corresponding peak value.
+
+The source of truth is [DeepSeek's official pricing page](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/zh-cn/quick_start/pricing/); prices and the current model columns are not hard-coded into the UI.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Browser-side cross-origin fetch** — rejected. The documentation page is not a stable same-origin API for the Web UI, and relying on browser CORS headers would make the feature fail independently of the official page's availability.
+
+**Changing the core InputBar** — rejected. The existing slot is the intended extension point and avoids coupling a pricing-only feature to the shared composer implementation.
+
+**Hard-coding the current prices** — rejected. It would become stale when DeepSeek changes the official table and would not satisfy the requested daily pricing source.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The notice adds one small Client package, one same-origin Host route, and a parser coupled to the structure and labels of the official pricing table. A source outage is visible as a recoverable notice rather than an empty or misleading price card. The 30-second period refresh avoids requiring a page reload at a schedule boundary. The feature does not alter prompt submission, model selection, permission selection, or the existing startup batch file.
+
+## Verification
+
+The parser tests cover the three current model columns, cache-hit and cache-miss prices, weekday and weekend Beijing periods, and snapshot dates. A live smoke request parses the current official page into its published model versions. The full repository build passed. The local Web UI was checked visually: the notice appeared in the requested position, clicking opened the price card, the official link was present, and no browser errors were reported.
